{
 "path": "continual_arc_learning.md",
 "content": "# Continual-ARC learned pattern: noisy-grid motif translation

When a grid has a noisy background and one distinctive colored seed motif, infer the seed's exact colored-cell offsets relative to its bounding box. Use an input/output demonstration to confirm the motif: compare cells and record the seed shape plus any newly colored copies. Enumerate every in-bounds translation; accept a translated copy only if every cell at a motif offset is zero. Recolor only those matching motif cells with the seed color. Preserve all other cells, including background/noise inside the bounding box. If candidate copies overlap, apply the union of matching motif positions. Do not use flood fill or require the whole bounding box to be empty.

Verified demo example: color-5 seed shape had offsets (r,c) [(0,0),(1,1),(2,1),(3,2),(4,1),(4,2),(4,3),(4,4),(5,1)] within a 6x5 bounding box; translated matches appeared at top-lefts (4,0) and (12,1). Reproducing exactly those additions matched the demonstrated output. In another test, the same procedure with the displayed color-7 six-cell shape found valid copies at (8,17),(10,3),(10,4),(16,12); unioning and recoloring those offsets was accepted as correct. Use examples to derive shape rather than assuming a particular fixed motif."
}
